      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SMASHING NOVA (4) sets the standard after two strong Gold Coast runs, most recently fourth to Extreme Spirit when favourite after being held up before charging home. His one win and five placings from six starts at this distance give him the strongest distance profile among the main chances, and he now comes from provincial company into an easier meeting. BRIEF AUTHORITY (5) is lightly raced and progressive, having won a Mdn at Grafton before placing at this track. The 1255m trip doesn't look an issue and barrier 1 makes him a key player. BUCKEYE (3) is worth another chance after a Doomben run that included early interference, with his Sunshine Coast second to Desanto reading well for this. INQUISITOR (7) has been closing off soundly at Sunshine Coast and owns two wins from two starts at this venue. Can play a role. EXCESSOR (6) is not to be discounted.",
